        <briefdescription>
<para>Check that an override of getMaximumWaveSpeed() keeps the contract of the base class&apos; default. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A material overrides getMaximumWaveSpeed() with a closed form to avoid the default&apos;s full constitutive evaluation. The artificial bulk viscosity&apos;s damage degradation divides the wave speed at the current non-local field by the one at a zero field, so an override that ignores the field returns the same speed for both: the ratio is 1 and the degradation silently does nothing. This function compares the override to the default (called non-virtually on the same object) at every given field, and checks that neither touches the state. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nNonlocalVariables</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of non-local variables of the material. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">material</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The material whose override is checked. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">currentResponse</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A response, including its state variables, at which to evaluate both. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">fields</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The non-local fields to evaluate at; they should include fields at which the material is damaged, at least one of them non-zero. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">relativeTolerance</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>0, the default, demands the bits of the default. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::runtime_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if the override differs from the default or changes the state variables. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
